 "summary": "Functoriality and cancellation of signed point twists are new to both Tau Ceti and Mathlib, and the PR reuses the existing bundle-map helpers (`bundleDiffeomorph`, `contMDiff_hom_bundle_iff`, `contMDiff_bundleMap_of_constant_coordinates`, `contMDiffAt_hom_bundle`) wherever they apply. Building the cancellation diffeomorphism and the restricted-scalars fibre equivalence by hand is justified: `bundleDiffeomorph` needs finite dimensionality, and Mathlib's `ContinuousLinearEquiv.restrictScalars` only covers maps from a space to itself.",
